# Audit source-backed distant-object transforms

Audit distant-object transforms from source evidence instead of accepting
manual editor placement as world-layout authority.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Audit distant-object transforms from source evidence instead of accepting
  manual editor placement as world-layout authority.

## Dependencies

No explicit task dependency was recorded in the legacy TODO.

## Evidence

World placement is derived from authored scenegraph transforms before mesh
publication. The former Blender-oriented distant-island splitter has been
removed because its one-unit proximity threshold was not source identity
evidence. Disconnected components now remain in their decoded source mesh at
any distance; source owner and placement records govern independent object
roles. Focused regressions require both near and distant components to preserve
source mesh ownership, positions, and UVs.

Nested source transforms still place drawables at their authored global
position, and narrative map-family grouping adds no spatial offset. The
generated world transform manifest keeps Unreal import translation and rotation
at zero and scale at one, so manual editor placement is not a second
world-layout authority.

Definition-only review meshes may receive deterministic gallery placement below
`review/`, but that namespace is excluded from the normal world import set and
therefore cannot alter production distant-object transforms.
